Bugfix: Add text alternatives to the avatar icons in the external storage picker

The "Available for" picker of the external storage settings builds two images in
JavaScript that carried no alt attribute, so they entered the accessibility tree
unnamed and screen readers fell back to the file name of the icon.

The two images needed different treatment. The icon next to the "All users"
shortcut only repeats the adjacent visible text and is now marked decorative.
The icon on a group result carries real information: unlike formatSelection, the
result list does not append "(group)" to the name, so the icon was the only thing
telling a group apart from a user of the same name. That result now marks the
image decorative and appends the already translated "(group)" as visually hidden
text, giving the entry the same wording it gets once selected.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 1.1.1
